    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos** headlining our active lineup. **Gunnar Henderson** secures the top score of 62.61 despite a neutral platoon disadvantage against Weathers, as his elite spot in the order and a favorable 16% park factor override the minor SP skill penalty. Furthermore, the slow delivery profile of the opposing pitcher grants a subtle boost to his stolen base ceiling\u2014a critical factor for our scarcity-weighted strategy. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Sasaki (5.30 xERA), with his 19% SP skill advantage propelling him to a strong 61.69 efficiency score. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** remain integral to our offensive core, they face a tough task today against the stifling 2.60 xERA of McDonald, forcing us to rely on their elite base projections to maintain competitiveness.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was keeping **Josh Jung** (46.79) out of the starting nine. While **Josh Jung** projects as a viable start, he simply fell behind the combined efficiency of our middle-of-the-order anchors. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, as his return remains vital to anchoring our outfield depth. We are also tracking the absence of **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** today due to team off-days, which limits our tactical flexibility. Managers should remain cautious regarding **Andy Pages**; while his score of 42.81 puts him in the lineup, his exposure to McDonald\u2019s elite pitching provides the narrowest margin for error among our starters today.",
